{"SUV":{"id":"83d6c22e-f762-4fd8-9933-757aeae399a3","word":"SUV","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"sport utility vehicle","word":"SUV"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"A man dressed as a lab tech, his blue scrubs startlingly pale against the vivid red and black chaos, moved into sight from behind the SUV. He carried an assault rifle.","ref":"2014, Jeff Jacobson, Growth, page 23:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[134,137]],"id":"e5f92759-fa7c-44f9-abc4-de8edc7d240c"},{"text":"As SUVs are higher and heavier, they are more likely to kill the people they hit. Driving an SUV in an urban area is an antisocial act.","ref":"2019 March 7, George Monbiot, “Cars are killing us. Within 10 years, we must phase them out”, in The Guardian:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[3,6],[3,7],[93,96]],"id":"eb92279c-bb62-447f-9832-b2f6a6791a60"},{"text":"Audi, which markets a variety of electrified S.U.V.s like the E-tron, is developing other designs as pure electrics, said an Audi of America spokesman, Mark Dahncke.","ref":"2021 February 4, Stephen Williams, “E.V.s Force Carmakers to Reinvent the Wheel, and Brakes, and Mirrors …”, in The New York Times, archived from the original on 12 Feb 2021:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[45,52]],"id":"c0874172-8a75-4886-a762-0bb6629dcf1e"},{"text":"For the whole year, the exotic automaker sold 7,430 cars and SUVs, down 9.5% compared to 2019. But the last quarter of 2020 was the best in the Italian supercar maker’s history and its order banks are already filled for the first nine months of 2021, Lamborghini CEO Stephan Winkelmann said.","ref":"2021 April 1, Peter Valdes-Dapena, “Sales of Bentleys and Lamborghinis are booming because rich people are bored”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[61,65]],"id":"58eb6f83-6f05-49cf-83b0-7bac8269b73f"}],"wikidata":["Q192152"],"senseid":["en:Q192152"],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with